# Credentials for the runtime daemon, loaded by `otter start`.
#
# One file for the whole project, because the daemon's environment is one
# process environment. An integration receives only the names its own manifest
# lists under `secrets:`.
#
# Copy to otter.env (gitignored) and fill in:
#
#   cp otter.env.example otter.env && chmod 600 otter.env
#
# Never put a value here that you would paste into a chat log, and never in an
# integration's otter.yaml -- `otter inspect` prints that in full.

# --- required: Freesound ----------------------------------------------------
# From https://freesound.org/apiv2/apply -- the "Client secret / API key".
# Authenticates search and MP3 preview downloads.
#FREESOUND_API_KEY=

# --- optional: Freesound original-quality downloads -------------------------
# Only needed when freesound/otter.yaml sets DOWNLOAD_FORMAT: original. The
# refresh token comes from the one-time OAuth2 flow (see README.md). Without
# these, the integration downloads MP3 previews, which need no OAuth2.
# FREESOUND_API_KEY doubles as the OAuth2 client secret, so it is not repeated
# here; set FREESOUND_CLIENT_SECRET only if the two values ever differ.
#FREESOUND_CLIENT_ID=
#FREESOUND_REFRESH_TOKEN=
#FREESOUND_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- note: Freesound destination --------------------------------------------
# DOWNLOAD_DIR is set in freesound/otter.yaml, not here. A manifest `env:` value
# always wins over this file, so setting it here would be ignored.

# --- optional: operational knobs --------------------------------------------
# The daemon's whole environment reaches the child process, so a knob works
# here without touching the manifest. Where otter.yaml also defines a key, the
# manifest wins. For example, a rehearsal that logs what it would do and writes
# nothing:
#DRY_RUN=0
